---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
const updated = '2026-10-05';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on PlantCare101: Microsoft Clarity and Google GA4" description="Cookies on PlantCare101: Microsoft Clarity and Google Analytics 4 load without a banner; what each cookie does, how long it lasts and how to block them." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Cookies', path: route('cookies', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Cookies</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <p>This page lists the cookies set when you visit PlantCare101 and explains how to block them. It complements the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>The plant tools need none</h2>
    <p>The watering calculator, the pet-safe plant checker, the light finder, the fertilizer dilution calculator and the diagnosis tool run in your browser. The plant, pot size, light and season you choose are kept in the page itself, and in the address bar when you use the share link of the watering calculator, never in a cookie. The only cookies on the site come from the audience measurement below.</p>
    <h2>Audience measurement</h2>
    <h3>Microsoft Clarity</h3>
    <p>Clarity loads as soon as a page opens; the site shows no consent banner. It tells us how the plant guides and tools are really used, through session recordings (clicks, scrolling, movement on the page) and heatmaps. What you type into fields, such as a plant name in the pet-safe checker, is masked in your browser before anything is sent. Cookies set: <code>_clck</code> (one year) and <code>_clsk</code> (one day); Microsoft may also set <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> on its own domains.</p>
    <h3>Google Analytics 4</h3>
    <p>Google Analytics 4, provided by Google Ireland Limited, loads the same way, without a banner. It counts page views and shows where visits come from, how long they last, which kind of device is used and the approximate location. Cookies set: <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_E9EV1P52L4</code>, two years each. Data is kept for 14 months.</p>
    <h3>Advertising and social media</h3>
    <p>The site shows no advertising and loads no social media button, so no advertising cookie is set.</p>
    <h2>The embedded calculator</h2>
    <p>The iframe version of the watering calculator offered to other websites loads neither Clarity nor Google Analytics and sets no cookie.</p>
    <h2>How to block these cookies</h2>
    <p>To object to audience measurement, block third-party cookies or the clarity.ms and google-analytics.com domains in your browser or with a content blocker, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. Then clear this site’s data to delete cookies already set. Every guide and tool keeps working without them.</p>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Last updated: {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
